  "notes": "Views identified as a bent sheet-metal angle bracket: front/top views show overall width and holes; side view shows depth profile with sloped side plates and rear upright; isometric confirms two base feet, side webs, and rear vertical plate with large circular through hole. Modeled as multibody plate approximation in a shared frame X=116 width, Y=105 height, Z=100 depth. Default sheet thickness is 3 mm and inside bend radius R5 per notes, but several edge returns/side lips are dimensioned 8/12 mm; complex bent/sloped sheet geometry and bend radii are approximated by rectangular plates. Large Ø82 through hole is encoded as a cut cylinder through the rear vertical plate, centered on X=58 and estimated Y=56 from the 50 mm center dimension in the front view plus base flange; z position through rear plate estimated. Two Ø12 through holes in horizontal front feet are cut along Y, centers at x=35 and 81 by symmetry, z=25 estimated from top/front view callout; through length extended to ensure cut. Top U-shaped/front return with R7 six places approximated as plates; six rounded corners and sloped side outline not fully represented by box bodies. Question/tolerance note in title block is mass tolerance ±1 g, not dimensional tolerance; provisional ±0.1 mm used for dimensions without explicit tolerances."
